# Bibliography (currently disabled)

The report has **no bibliography and no `\cite{}` commands** until the team deliberately re-enables them.

When bibliography is turned back on:

1. Save each source under `reference/sources/{citekey}.pdf` (or allowed alternative).
2. Add a verified BibTeX entry in `biblio.bib` with `file = {reference/sources/...}`.
3. Uncomment `\addbibresource{biblio.bib}` in `tpl/isipfe.cls` and `\printbibliography` in `main.tex`.
4. Only then add `\cite{...}` in the report.

If a source cannot be downloaded and checked, **do not cite it**.

Never mention Cursor rules or download policy in report `.tex` text.
